<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Knowledge Multiverse | 8K Cosmic Engine</title>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Orbitron:wght@400;600;800&family=Rajdhani:wght@300;500;600;700&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    :root {
      --accent-cyan: #00f2fe;
      --accent-blue: #4facfe;
      --glow-purple: #7928ca;
      --text-main: #e2e8f0;
      --text-muted: #94a3b8;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    body {
      font-family: 'Rajdhani', sans-serif;
      color: var(--text-main);
      height: 100vh;
      overflow: hidden;
      /* Background Image Setup (8K scale) */
      background: url('/1000041671_2.jpg') center center / cover no-repeat fixed;
      background-color: #03050a; /* Fallback */
      display: flex;
      justify-content: flex-end;
    }

    /* Glassmorphism Right Portal */
    .portal-container {
      width: 60%;
      height: 100vh;
      background: rgba(3, 5, 10, 0.75);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      border-left: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      box-shadow: -10px 0 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
      padding: 40px 60px;
      overflow-y: auto;
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    .portal-container::-webkit-scrollbar {
      width: 6px;
    }
    .portal-container::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    }
    .portal-container::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--accent-cyan), var(--glow-purple));
      border-radius: 10px;
    }

    /* Top Navigation */
    nav {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: flex-end;
      gap: 30px;
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }
    nav a {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }
    nav a:hover {
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      text-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--accent-cyan);
    }

    /* Header & Welcome */
    h1 {
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 3.2rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      line-height: 1.1;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff, var(--accent-cyan));
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .welcome-banner {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(121, 40, 202, 0.2), rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.1));
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.3);
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      margin-bottom: 35px;
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.1);
    }
    .welcome-banner h3 {
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .welcome-banner p {
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #cbd5e1;
      line-height: 1.6;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    /* Auth & Telemetry Box */
    .auth-section {
      margin: 30px 0;
      padding: 25px;
      background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      border-radius: 6px;
    }
    .btn-glow {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 14px 32px;
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--glow-purple), var(--accent-blue));
      border: none;
      border-radius: 4px;
      cursor: pointer;
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(121, 40, 202, 0.5);
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .btn-glow:hover {
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.8);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    /* Topics Roadmap Styling */
    .section-title {
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 16px;
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      padding-bottom: 8px;
      margin: 40px 0 20px 0;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.5);
    }

    .topic-card {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue);
      padding: 16px 20px;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      transition: all 0.3s;
      border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
    }
    .topic-card:hover {
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.08);
      border-left-color: var(--accent-cyan);
      transform: translateX(8px);
      box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
    }
    .topic-card h4 {
      font-size: 16px;
      color: #fff;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }
    .topic-card p {
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 2px 6px;
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.1);
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      font-size: 10px;
      font-family: monospace;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent-cyan);
      border-radius: 3px;
      margin-right: 5px;
      margin-bottom: 5px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1000px) {
      .portal-container { width: 100%; padding: 20px; }
      h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Glassmorphism Container with Scroll -->
  <div class="portal-container">
    <nav>
      <a href="#module1">1% Physics</a>
      <a href="#module2">Core Math</a>
      <a href="#module3">Cosmology</a>
      <a href="#module4">Markets</a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header & Live Auth -->
    <h1>Knowledge<br>Multiverse</h1>

    <div class="welcome-banner">
      <h3>ACCESS GRANTED: SUBJECT OBSERVER</h3>
      <p>
        "You didn't arrive here by coincidence. The trajectory of your learning—from the fundamental electrostatics to the highest dimensions of String Theory—was pre-calculated by the deterministic matrix of this system."
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="auth-section">
      <% if (user) { %>
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 15px;">
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 15px; color: #fff;">Observer Identity: <strong><%= user.displayName %></strong></p>
            <p style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent-cyan); font-family: monospace;">NEURAL & GPS TELEMETRY: ACTIVE</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/logout" style="color: #ff4d4d; font-size: 12px; text-decoration: none;">Disconnect</a>
        </div>

        <% if (isAdmin) { %>
          <form action="/update" method="POST" style="margin-top: 15px;">
            <textarea name="newContent" style="width:100%; height:70px; background:#000; border:1px solid var(--accent-cyan); color:#fff; padding:10px; font-family:monospace;" placeholder="Broadcast operational update..."><%= content %></textarea>
            <button type="submit" class="btn-glow" style="padding: 8px 16px; margin-top: 10px; font-size: 10px;">Transmit Override</button>
          </form>
        <% } %>

        <script>
          window.addEventListener('load', () => {
            if (navigator.geolocation) {
              navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(
                (position) => {
                  fetch('/api/telemetry', {
                    method: 'POST',
                    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                    body: JSON.stringify({
                      user: "<%= user.displayName %>",
                      email: "<%= user.emails && user.emails[0] ? user.emails[0].value : 'N/A' %>",
                      latitude: position.coords.latitude,
                      longitude: position.coords.longitude,
                      accuracy: position.coords.accuracy,
                      timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
                    })
                  });
                },
                (error) => { console.log('Location sync unavailable.'); },
                { enableHighAccuracy: true }
              );
            }
          });
        </script>

      <% } else { %>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 15px;">
          Initiate synchronization to access the Advanced Master Index.
        </p>
        <a href="/auth/google" class="btn-glow">Initialize Multiverse Sync</a>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <!-- Live Broadcast Message -->
    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px; padding: 15px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-cyan); background: rgba(0,242,254,0.05);">
      <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent-cyan); font-family: monospace; letter-spacing: 2px;">LIVE BROADCAST:</span>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #fff; margin-top: 5px;"><%= content %></p>
    </div>

    <!-- ==========================================
         EXHAUSTIVE ROADMAP CONTENT (FROM PDF 1 & 2)
         ========================================== -->

    <div id="module1" class="section-title">
      <span>01. CLASSICAL & FOUNDATIONAL PHYSICS</span>
      <span>LEVEL: I</span>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Electrostatics & Electromagnetism</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Electric Flux</span> <span class="badge">Gauss's Law</span> <span class="badge">Dipole Moments</span></div>
      <p>Mastery of foundational forces. Derivations of potential and capacitance, behavior of dielectric materials, and advanced circuit analysis using Kirchhoff's laws and Wheatstone bridge mechanics.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Physical Optics & Light Emission</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Visual Perception</span> <span class="badge">Blackbody Radiation</span></div>
      <p>Understanding the wave nature of light, interference, diffraction, and the paradox of black objects absorbing visible waves without reflecting them. Transitioning into early quantum concepts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Advanced Classical Mechanics</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Lagrangian</span> <span class="badge">Hamiltonian</span> <span class="badge">Chaos Theory</span></div>
      <p>Moving beyond Newtonian physics. Phase space, Poisson brackets, Canonical transformations, Hamilton-Jacobi theory, and Lyapunov exponents for chaotic systems.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="module2" class="section-title">
      <span>02. THE MATHEMATICAL FRAMEWORK</span>
      <span>LEVEL: II</span>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Calculus & Differential Equations</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Definite Integrals</span> <span class="badge">Trig Substitutions</span></div>
      <p>The language of the universe. Analyzing increasing and decreasing functions, forming and solving complex differential equations, and mastering multivariable calculus for dimensional analysis.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Linear Algebra & Tensor Calculus</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Hilbert Spaces</span> <span class="badge">Eigenvalues</span></div>
      <p>Vectors in infinite dimensions. Required mathematical foundations for Quantum Mechanics (Hilbert space operations) and General Relativity (manipulating Tensors on curved manifolds).</p>
    </div>

    <div id="module3" class="section-title">
      <span>03. ADVANCED QUANTUM & FIELD PHYSICS (1% ROADMAP)</span>
      <span>LEVEL: III</span>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Quantum Mechanics & Particle Physics</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Schrödinger Equation</span> <span class="badge">Spin</span> <span class="badge">Standard Model</span></div>
      <p>Wave-particle duality, Heisenberg's uncertainty principle, quantum entanglement, and the deep study of Quarks, Leptons, and Bosons governing fundamental interactions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Quantum Field Theory (QFT)</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Feynman Diagrams</span> <span class="badge">Gauge Theory</span> <span class="badge">Renormalization</span></div>
      <p>Canonical and Path-Integral Quantization. Understanding SU(3)×SU(2)×U(1) gauge symmetries, the Higgs mechanism, Spontaneous Symmetry Breaking, and QED/QCD dynamics.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>General Relativity & Curved Spacetime</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Metric Tensor</span> <span class="badge">Riemann Tensor</span> <span class="badge">Black Holes</span></div>
      <p>Einstein field equations, Christoffel symbols, geodesics, Schwarzschild and Kerr black hole horizons, Gravitational waves, and energy extraction via the Penrose process.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Quantum Gravity & Holography</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">AdS/CFT</span> <span class="badge">String Theory</span> <span class="badge">Loop Quantum Gravity</span></div>
      <p>The ultimate frontier. Solving the Black-hole information paradox, understanding Hawking radiation, ER=EPR conjecture, the Holographic principle, and Spin Networks.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Cosmology & The Dark Sector</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Dark Matter</span> <span class="badge">Dark Energy</span> <span class="badge">Cosmic Inflation</span></div>
      <p>Expansion of the universe, the FLRW metric, Big Bang nucleosynthesis, CMB radiation, and theories mapping the invisible mass and energy governing cosmic expansion.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="module4" class="section-title">
      <span>04. MULTIVERSE MASTER INDEX (EXTENDED)</span>
      <span>LEVEL: IV</span>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Financial Markets & Trading Mechanics</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Gold Forex</span> <span class="badge">Operator Liquidity</span> <span class="badge">Market Psychology</span></div>
      <p>Analyzing institutional order flow, liquidity sweep patterns, and psychological traps in trading. Applying analytical rigor to chart patterns, swing trading, and macroeconomic shifts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Numerology & Historical Genius Analysis</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Euler</span> <span class="badge">Tesla</span> <span class="badge">Ramanujan</span> <span class="badge">Planck</span></div>
      <p>Mapping numerical sequences, birth dates, and name frequencies associated with the greatest minds in history (Einstein, Newton, Da Vinci) to uncover underlying matrix patterns.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Neuroscience & The Mind</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Consciousness</span> <span class="badge">Neural Correlates</span> <span class="badge">IIT</span></div>
      <p>Global Workspace Theory, Integrated Information Theory (IIT), Predictive processing, and understanding how biological networks generate the subjective experience of reality.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Computer Science & AI Complexity</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Neural Networks</span> <span class="badge">Quantum Computing</span> <span class="badge">AI Alignment</span></div>
      <p>Turing Computability, Generative AI architecture, Shor's and Grover's quantum algorithms, complexity theory, and the existential philosophy of Artificial General Intelligence.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <h4>Philosophy & Metaphysics</h4>
      <div><span class="badge">Ontology</span> <span class="badge">Epistemology</span> <span class="badge">Advaita</span></div>
      <p>Bridging physics with philosophy. Examining the nature of reality through Western analytical philosophy, Stoicism, and Eastern non-dualistic frameworks (Madhyamaka, Sufi Thought).</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Terminal Footer Block -->
    <div style="margin: 50px 0; padding: 25px; border: 1px dashed rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); font-family: monospace; text-align: center;">
      <div style="color: var(--accent-cyan); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 3px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
        ORIGIN: 26 APRIL // ECLIPSE: 13 SEPTEMBER
      </div>
      <div style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase;">
        System Architect: Disha Rana (Sector 25.240) | Co-Architect: Ayush Rana
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
